  "notes": [
    "Works are left out, in this order, if: the title is missing or marks a non-research item (editorials, errata, retractions, calls for papers); the work repeats one already kept; the title marks a book review or front matter (award notices, lists of reviewers, editors' comments); its DOI is missing or not under the journal's publisher prefixes (config/fields.json doiPrefixes), which drops preprint copies and same-named journals that OpenAlex filed under ours; it has no abstract of at least 100 characters, which drops book reviews and front matter; or it comes from a split journal and its topic maps to none of the five fields.",
    "Multi-field journals are split by OpenAlex primary-topic subfield (config/fields.json splitRule); these topic labels are automated and imperfect.",
    "OpenAlex and Crossref change over time, so a later rebuild can differ slightly; compare corpus/ids.txt and idsSha256."
